From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:11:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: bridge: withdraw the old port before FDB replacement

A userspace FDB replacement can move a static peer between independent
switches. Notify switchdev of the old destination before changing fdb->dst,
matching the existing learned-station move sequence. A new-port ADD alone
can leave a static entry in the previous ASIC, blackholing later traffic
even though the software FDB and new ASIC agree.

Observed on BE3600 P8 with its two independent RTL8372 trees: moving a
sticky VID 100 entry from LAN1 to LAN5 leaves LAN1 self static until the
old ASIC receives the missing delete. Do not pin a CPU FDB entry as a
workaround or clear unrelated VLAN/MAC entries.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -1223,6 +1223,8 @@
 			return -EEXIST;
 
 		if (READ_ONCE(fdb->dst) != source) {
+			/* The old switch may be independent of the new one. */
+			br_switchdev_fdb_notify(br, fdb, RTM_DELNEIGH);
 			WRITE_ONCE(fdb->dst, source);
 			modified = true;
 		}
